# Proposed title of this feature request

Allow reducing serviceNodePortRange to a smaller range

# What is the nature and description of the request?

As noted in the documentation [here|https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.20/html/configuring_network_settings/configuring-node-port-service-range#nw-nodeport-service-range-edit_configuring-node-port-service-range], the serviceNodePortRange can be configured on the cluster with a patch command.

{noformat}oc patch network.config.openshift.io cluster --type=merge -p \
  '{
    "spec":
      { "serviceNodePortRange": "<port_range>" }
  }'{noformat}

The same [documentation|https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.20/html/configuring_network_settings/configuring-node-port-service-range#nw-nodeport-service-range-edit_configuring-node-port-service-range] notes the following:

{quote}You can expand the range on either side, but you cannot shrink it after installation.{quote}

This means that if this value is misconfigured, it can lead to serious issues with the cluster such as [https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/OCPBUGS-77769|https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/OCPBUGS-77769|smart-link]. 

The [documentation|https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.20/html/configuring_network_settings/configuring-node-port-service-range#nw-nodeport-service-range-edit_configuring-node-port-service-range] recommends to reinstall the cluster if an issue like this happens. 

{quote}If you expanded the range and a port allocation issue occurs, create a new cluster and set the required range for it.{quote}

Allowing the serviceNodePortRange to be reduced will be a better alternative to this.

Why does the customer need this? (List the business requirements here)

Having to reinstall the cluster can take significant time and effort for customers. 

# List any affected packages or components.

Cluster-network-operator, Openshift-kube-apiserver

